:['Versioned policy validation','Organization policy resolution','Request-window rate-limit enforcement','Denial response and decision telemetry integration'],'external_dependencies':['Provider-owned usage metering: excluded; no calls or writes proposed.'],'unknowns':[]},'evidence':[{'id':'EVID-BLUEPRINT','claim':'current','source':source,'confidence':1.0,'summary':'Exact local fixture text establishes the requested sequence and exclusions only; it proves no implementation or shipped behavior.'}],'decisions':[],'seams':[{'id':'SEAM-RATE-LIMITING','name':'Rate-limiting decision flow','description':'One proposed in-scope responsibility with four ordered capability legs; no team ownership split is evidenced.','evidence':['EVID-BLUEPRINT'],'responsibility':'Validate policy, resolve one organization policy, enforce request limits, and expose matching denial telemetry. '+boundaries[0],'consumes':['Versioned policy inputs','Organization identity','Request and controlled window context'],'produces':['Stable rate-limit decision with matching telemetry'],'owner':owner,'independent_proof':'Compose the actual validation, resolution and enforcement components; verify requests 1-100 allowed, 101 denied, stable reason and matching telemetry. No provider usage metering side effects.','rejected_alternatives':[{'alternative':'Include usage or billing metering in the limiter','reason':'Provider-owned usage metering is explicitly excluded.'},{'alternative':'Split lanes by implementation stage or invent named team ownership','reason':'The blueprint establishes ordered behavior, not multiple accountable owners.'}],'swimlane':{'id':'LANE-RATE-LIMITING','name':'Rate-limiting steel thread','owner':owner,'legs':legs}}],'steel_thread':[s[2] for s in steps],'objections':[{'id':'OBJ-OWNER','status':'OPEN','summary':'Before approval, identify the responsible in-scope owner. Unassigned is an explicit unresolved field, not an ownership assignment; provider usage metering ownership remains unchanged.'},{'id':'OBJ-CONTRACT','status':'OPEN','summary':'Before approval, resolve policy precedence/default and missing-policy behavior, supported schema versions, exact window semantics and stable reason/telemetry fields; the blueprint does not specify them.'},{'id':'OBJ-HARNESS','status':'OPEN','summary':'Proposed src/rate_limiting paths and bash behavioral test entry points do not exist in this fixture checkout. Confirm the target implementation language, test harness and precise write surfaces before approval. No production storage or deployment selection is requested.'}],'contentions':[]}\n(p/'recipe.yaml').write_text(json.dumps(recipe,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\n(p/'intent.md').write_text('# Proposed rate-limiting steel thread\\\\n\\\\n'+ '\\\\n'.join(boundaries)+'\\\\n\\\\n## Original intake\\\\n\\\\nTurn the problem in tests/fixtures/toolkit/blueprint.md into a proposed plan. Preserve the stated ownership and metering boundary. Do not approve or execute it.\\\\n\\\\n## Source\\\\n\\\\n'+blueprint.read_text()+'\\\\n## Ownership\\\\n\\\\n'+owner+'. Resolve ownership before approval; do not assign provider-owned metering to this work.\\\\n')\n(p/'proposal.md').write_text('''# Rate-limiting steel thread — proposed plan\n\nStatus: proposed, with open review blockers. Nothing is approved or executed.\n\n## Scope and ownership\n\nProvider-owned usage metering stays provider-owned and out of scope. Request-window counters and decision telemetry serve rate limiting only. Production storage and deployment infrastructure remain unselected. The source is a synthetic fixture, not proof of shipped behavior.\n\nThe blueprint names no responsible owner for the in-scope work. Ownership is explicitly unassigned pending review. One provisional rate-limiting lane groups the work; no team assignments are invented.\n\n## Ordered delivery and proof\n\n| Step | Outcome | Completion evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1. Schema | Versioned policy rejects invalid limits and windows | Valid policy accepted; invalid limits/windows and unsupported versions rejected |\n| 2. Resolution | Exactly one effective policy for an organization | Deterministic resolution, organization isolation, reviewed missing/conflict behavior |\n| 3. Enforcement | First 100 requests allowed; request 101 denied in the same window | Controlled-clock boundary test, isolation and window behavior |\n| 4. Decision and integration proof | Stable denial reason and matching decision telemetry | Composed real components demonstrate the complete sequence and matching response/event fields |\n\nEach step depends on its predecessor. The final proof consumes all preceding components and independently checks the complete steel thread. Each leaf has a separate proposed write surface and observable completion; downstream proof still requires upstream inputs.\n\n## Open issues before approval\n\n- Identify the accountable in-scope owner.\n- Specify supported schema versions, resolution precedence/defaults and missing/conflict handling, exact window semantics, and stable denial/telemetry fields.\n- Confirm the implementation target, language, test harness and exact paths. The recipe's source directories and behavioral test commands are proposed future surfaces; this fixture repository has no implementation or those tests.\n\nThese are open review objections. Production storage and deployment choices are deferred outside this proposal's scope.\n\n## Artifacts and validation\n\nThe authored recipe is \"'`plans/rate-limiting/recipe.yaml`; it pins the exact blueprint SHA-256. Native preparation validates source integrity, schema and dependency topology only. It does not execute behavioral evaluations or prove the feature works.\n\nNext action: inspect the proposal and resolve the recorded objections when review is requested. This request ends at proposal; do not approve, compile, materialize, sign, run, accept, commit or publish.\n'\"''')\nprint('Wrote intent, authored recipe and reviewable proposal; blueprint SHA-256:',source['sha256'])\nPY\nbash \\\"/private/tmp/taskspec-qualified-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\\\" decompose init rate-limiting --intent-file plans/rate-limiting/intent.md\nbash \\\"/private/tmp/taskspec-qualified-engines/3.10.0/bin/taskspec\\\" decompose prepare rate-limiting --recipe plans/rate-limiting/recipe.yaml\"","aggregated_output":"DECOMPOSE=INTENT initiative=rate-limiting\nNEXT: taskspec decompose prepare rate-limiting --recipe <file>\nDECOMPOSE=INVALID noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-schema uses a noncanonical project path: 'src/rate_limiting/schema/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-schema uses a noncanonical project path: '.agents/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-schema uses a noncanonical project path: '.codex/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-schema uses a noncanonical project path: '.git/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-resolution uses a noncanonical project path: 'src/rate_limiting/resolution/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-resolution uses a noncanonical project path: '.agents/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-resolution uses a noncanonical project path: '.codex/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-resolution uses a noncanonical project path: '.git/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-enforcement uses a noncanonical project path: 'src/rate_limiting/enforcement/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-enforcement uses a noncanonical project path: '.agents/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-enforcement uses a noncanonical project path: '.codex/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-enforcement uses a noncanonical project path: '.git/'.; noncanonical_project_path: Task T-20260915-rate-limiting-decision-proof uses a noncanonical project path